    suggested_answer: 'The standards of procedural due process (the "Twin-Notice Rule") that should have been observed are:\n\n1. First Notice: A written notice served on the employee specifying the ground or grounds for termination (in this case, abandonment or gross and habitual neglect of duty), and giving said employee reasonable opportunity (at least 5 calendar days) within which to explain their side.\n\n2. Hearing/Conference: A hearing or conference during which the employee, with the assistance of counsel if desired, is given the opportunity to respond to the charge, present evidence, or rebut the evidence presented against them.\n\n3. Second Notice: A written notice of termination served on the employee, indicating that upon due consideration of all the circumstances, grounds have been established to justify the termination. Failure to observe these steps makes the dismissal procedurally infirm, even if a just cause exists.'
