    suggested_answer: 'Case A: Closure due to serious business losses\n1. Steps: (a) Serve a written notice on the workers and the DOLE at least one month before the intended date of closure; (b) Prove the serious business losses through audited financial statements.\n2. Separation Pay: No. Under Article 298 (formerly 283) of the Labor Code, separation pay is not required if the closure is due to serious business losses or financial reverses.\n\nCase B: Closure due to old age\n1. Legality: Yes, it is allowed as a valid exercise of management prerogative to close the business.\n2. Separation Benefits: Yes. The employees are entitled to separation pay equivalent to at least one (1) month pay or at least one-half (1/2) month pay for every year of service, whichever is higher. Closure due to old age is not considered closure due to serious business losses, hence the requirement for separation pay applies.'
